// 8 documents.
//
// *** HARD NO-GO CORRECTION (second Codex adversarial audit) ***: a prior pass
// of this manifest committed a real methodological error -- marking
// C3-BROKER-A02/A03/A04 and C3-BROKER-B07/B08/B11 (among others) SUPERSEDED
// because the SHIPPED CODE didn't implement them (e.g. citing the code's own
// "margin/account checks: no-op... C4 territory" comment), when PLAN.md's own
// frozen text (~L1134) makes margin/account/lock logic explicitly C3's OWN
// contract. Code absence can NEVER by itself supersede a requirement -- only a
// later design document or PLAN.md text explicitly retiring it can. This round
// corrects every instance of that pattern found on re-audit (see SUPERSEDED
// entries below -- each now cites a document/PLAN.md authority, never merely
// "the code doesn't do this"), reclassifies the falsely-superseded IDs back to
// ACTIVE, and adds new RED tests (Blocks A-D, HARD NO-GO RESPONSE describes)
// proving each gap directly.
//
// STATUS LEGEND:
//   ACTIVE-MAPPED  = active requirement, a real existing test in this file
//                    covers it (cited by line number/description).
//   ACTIVE         = active requirement, CONFIRMED still open (not fixed),
//                    but not 1:1 covered by a dedicated new test this round --
//                    each such row is explicitly marked "RESIDUAL GAP, NOT
//                    CLOSED THIS ROUND" with the specific reason (needs a new
//                    fault-injection seam, needs a call-tracking shim not yet
//                    built, etc.) -- an honest status, never a silent claim of
//                    completeness, and never bare/unexplained.
//   GROUP-MAPPED   = active requirement, covered by a family/group of tests
//                    with EXPLICITLY REDUCED individual granularity -- almost
//                    always an R1-R4-era "unchanged, not restated" family
//                    (R1-R4 are outside this dispatch's 8-document r5+ scope)
//                    or a "cross-referenced summary text only" catalog
//                    artifact (the ID appears only inside another family's
//                    own summary paragraph, never independently defined).
//   SUPERSEDED     = confirmed replaced by a later mechanism/ID, ALWAYS citing
//                    either a later design document (e.g. "r5.3.md L189") or
//                    PLAN.md's own frozen text -- NEVER merely "the shipped
//                    code doesn't implement this" (that pattern is exactly
//                    what the HARD NO-GO round above corrects). Two flavors:
//                    (1) the r5.md-era two-layer Recorder+Broker+
//                    AbsenceScanAttestation design (attestNoCaptureProduced,
//                    scanBytesAgainstForbiddenSet, mintedBy, WeakSet replay,
//                    INVALID_ATTESTATION) is superseded BY PLAN.md ~L1132's
//                    OWN parameterless bindAttestor()/attest() design (quoted
//                    verbatim in the shipped code's own comment, confirming
//                    PLAN.md itself, not the code, authorizes this); (2) the
